rivate coins were made illegal. ... The installation of Boulton\'s steam-powered machinery, coupled with a French invention, the \'reducing machine\', which reproduced original coin designs by machine rather than by hand engraving, enabled for the first time the mass production of high-quality and homogenous copper coins and transformed the Mint itself into an \'industrial concern\'. These changes coincided with the growth of a \'second\' British Empire and the Mint began producing more coins for overseas dependenies."'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 918, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 825})
